   "id": "niddah.57a.9",
   "daf": "57a",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "אֲבָל אֵין נֶאֱמָנִין לֹא עַל הַסְּכָכוֹת וְכוּ׳. סְכָכוֹת — דִּתְנַן: ״אֵלּוּ הֵן סְכָכוֹת — אִילָן הַמֵּיסֵךְ עַל הָאָרֶץ״. פְּרָעוֹת — דִּתְנַן: ״אֲבָנִים פְּרוּעוֹת הַיּוֹצְאוֹת מִן הַגָּדֵר״.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «But» with regard to the following cases in which the exact location of a grave is unknown, the Samaritans «are not deemed credible» to testify: They are «not» deemed credible to testify «about overhanging boughs,» nor about the protrusions that jut out of stone fences. The Gemara explains these terms: The term «overhanging boughs» should be understood «as we learned» in a mishna (Oholot 8:2): «These are overhanging boughs: A tree that hangs over the ground.» The term «protrusions» should be understood «as we learned» in the Tosefta (Oholot 9:4): «Protruding stones that jut out of a fence.»"
  }
 ],
